WEBVTT

00:56.389 --> 00:58.099
You guys alive?

00:59.851 --> 01:01.686
I can't hear you!

01:55.824 --> 01:57.742
How would you rate today's gig?

01:58.827 --> 02:00.036
Five hundred.

02:00.120 --> 02:02.497
- Five hundred? That's high!
- Maki rates a three.

02:03.289 --> 02:04.290
That's brutal!

02:06.000 --> 02:07.961
- That's hilarious.
- That's so brutal.

02:09.212 --> 02:11.464
It was great. Totally great.

02:11.548 --> 02:13.049
The audience was on fire.

02:15.385 --> 02:19.222
Okay, now let's decide who'll drive today.

02:20.431 --> 02:23.643
- On the count of three, point.
- Point?

02:23.726 --> 02:25.395
- Point on three.
- Okay.

02:25.478 --> 02:27.272
- The worst member?
- That's right.

02:27.355 --> 02:28.189
Thought so.

02:28.898 --> 02:30.316
- That'll be easy.
- Oh, shut up.

02:30.400 --> 02:31.985
- That'll be easy.
- Here goes.

02:33.611 --> 02:34.946
- Okay.
- Let's go.

02:35.446 --> 02:36.781
- One, two, three!
- One, two, three!

02:50.253 --> 02:52.422
We're the citizens of this country.

02:55.174 --> 02:56.384
The "citizens"?

02:56.467 --> 02:58.177
That's right. The citizens.

02:58.678 --> 03:01.681
That's insane. We're all humans.

03:01.764 --> 03:03.516
I wouldn't be so sure.

03:05.685 --> 03:07.520
I'm the leader of this team.

03:08.771 --> 03:10.523
We made this game.

03:10.607 --> 03:14.235
Incidentally,
it was developed by him, Shitara.

03:14.736 --> 03:17.947
But this will be
the first time it'll be played.

03:18.031 --> 03:20.450
We haven't even played it ourselves yet.

03:22.619 --> 03:24.287
In other words,

03:24.370 --> 03:27.582
we'll be playing against you,
the citizens, in this game?

03:27.665 --> 03:28.499
That's right.

03:29.000 --> 03:33.588
All the face card games are deathmatches
against the citizens of this land.

03:34.631 --> 03:36.507
The team that loses dies.

03:37.050 --> 03:38.051
In other words,

03:39.260 --> 03:43.514
these games are serious affairs
even for us citizens.

03:46.392 --> 03:47.685
Shall we begin?

03:49.354 --> 03:51.648
This is the game we are about to play.

03:53.691 --> 03:56.027
Difficulty, King of Clubs.

03:56.653 --> 03:57.570
Game…

03:58.863 --> 03:59.948
"Osmosis."

04:02.200 --> 04:03.743
"Osmosis."

05:21.571 --> 05:23.281
The rules are very simple.

05:25.491 --> 05:26.993
There's a two-hour time limit.

05:27.493 --> 05:29.620
We battle each other for points,

05:29.704 --> 05:32.790
and the team with the most points
at the end clears the game.

05:34.584 --> 05:36.919
Both teams start with 10,000 points each.

05:37.420 --> 05:41.257
You'll divide the points
between members before the game starts.

05:43.634 --> 05:47.305
They can be divided as you please,
but the least you can start with is 100.

05:48.014 --> 05:50.141
Talk it over carefully before you decide.

05:51.350 --> 05:55.271
The amount you start with
is extremely important in this game.

06:00.151 --> 06:01.736
Here's how you get points.

06:02.445 --> 06:05.782
There are three ways to get points.

06:06.407 --> 06:07.408
Battles.

06:08.034 --> 06:08.993
Items.

06:09.869 --> 06:10.703
Base.

06:11.204 --> 06:12.080
Wait.

06:12.580 --> 06:13.873
Sure. What's your question?

06:14.791 --> 06:16.459
This doesn't make any sense at all.

06:17.418 --> 06:18.252
Okay.

06:18.336 --> 06:20.421
Without an example,
it's probably hard to get.

06:21.422 --> 06:24.258
For now, I've given you
random amounts of points.

06:25.843 --> 06:28.763
The number on your wrist is
how many points you have.

06:30.598 --> 06:31.599
Let's start with battles.

06:33.059 --> 06:34.227
ARISU 2,000

06:34.310 --> 06:36.646
Battles are decided
by how many points you have.

06:38.689 --> 06:42.110
To battle someone,
you just need to touch your opponent.

06:42.193 --> 06:43.027
Hey!

06:43.611 --> 06:44.737
BATTLE

06:47.990 --> 06:49.575
NIRAGI: 2,000 LOSE

06:49.659 --> 06:50.576
KYUMA: 3,500 WIN

06:50.660 --> 06:52.245
The person who has more points wins.

06:52.745 --> 06:55.706
The winner gets 500 points from the loser.

06:55.790 --> 06:56.707
NIRAGI: 2,000 -500 LOSE

06:56.791 --> 06:57.834
NIRAGI: 1,500

06:57.917 --> 07:00.461
KYUMA: 3,500 +500 WIN

07:00.545 --> 07:02.255
KYUMA: 4,000

07:02.338 --> 07:05.508
There has been a change
in points for both teams.

07:09.846 --> 07:13.015
The King of Clubs Team
leads by 1,000 points.

07:21.983 --> 07:23.276
ARISU: 2,000

07:23.359 --> 07:26.320
So you don't know
your opponent's points until you battle.

07:26.404 --> 07:27.363
Right.

07:27.447 --> 07:30.992
This means battles are fought
without knowing each other's points,

07:31.075 --> 07:33.411
so it's a seriously risky fight.

07:33.911 --> 07:37.290
Also, multiple people can fight a battle.

07:37.915 --> 07:38.958
For example…

07:40.501 --> 07:42.587
You two, hold hands.

07:47.717 --> 07:49.093
What's this?

07:49.635 --> 07:51.012
Don't tell me you're blushing.

08:03.357 --> 08:05.359
You two make a nice couple.

08:07.737 --> 08:10.948
Anyway, when two teammates
are touching one another,

08:11.032 --> 08:13.284
they battle with the sum of their points,

08:13.367 --> 08:16.287
so they can defeat an opponent
that they can't defeat alone.

08:21.042 --> 08:23.628
Then when you win,
you each split the 500 points.

08:27.882 --> 08:28.883
Next…

08:30.218 --> 08:31.260
The items!

08:31.886 --> 08:33.721
ITEM

08:34.305 --> 08:38.893
Hidden somewhere
inside all these containers are six items.

08:41.812 --> 08:42.772
This place is huge!

08:42.855 --> 08:45.525
There are only six in this massive arena?

08:45.608 --> 08:48.903
You get extra points
when you touch the item.

08:49.737 --> 08:51.614
Now let me explain this.

08:51.697 --> 08:53.199
The key to making a comeback…

08:54.534 --> 08:55.493
is your base.

08:59.956 --> 09:01.666
This is your team's base.

09:02.166 --> 09:04.210
Ours is on the other side of the arena.

09:06.754 --> 09:09.549
If you touch the opposing team's base,

09:10.550 --> 09:12.260
you'll get 10,000 points.

09:12.343 --> 09:13.970
Ten thousand points?

09:14.470 --> 09:16.264
That's freaking insane!

09:16.347 --> 09:19.976
That's why you need to leave a keeper
to protect your base.

09:20.059 --> 09:25.189
When a player is touching their own base,
they have infinite points.

09:26.023 --> 09:26.983
Infinite?

09:28.609 --> 09:30.945
What if you battle someone
with infinite points?

09:34.699 --> 09:35.700
Come here a sec.

09:52.675 --> 09:54.427
ARISU: 2,250 LOSE
KYUMA: INFINITE WIN

09:54.510 --> 09:56.429
The loser loses 10,000 points.

09:56.512 --> 09:58.264
ARISU: -7,750 -10,000

09:58.347 --> 09:59.432
KYUMA: 3,500

09:59.515 --> 10:01.100
The winner gains 10,000 points.

10:01.976 --> 10:03.311
KYUMA: 3,500 +10,000

10:03.394 --> 10:05.354
KYUMA: 13,500

10:05.938 --> 10:07.023
Hold on here!

10:08.065 --> 10:11.986
What if you lose 10,000 points
and go below zero?

10:14.405 --> 10:15.781
You die.

10:18.951 --> 10:20.828
If you try to touch the other team's base,

10:20.911 --> 10:23.914
but their keeper blocks you
and touches you,

10:23.998 --> 10:25.374
you'll lose 10,000 points…

10:26.834 --> 10:27.918
and die.

10:28.502 --> 10:31.464
While the other team gets 10,000 points.

10:32.757 --> 10:34.008
That's way too risky!

10:34.091 --> 10:36.761
But if you succeed,
you'll come from behind and win.

10:40.389 --> 10:41.307
Incidentally,

10:42.308 --> 10:45.436
when players exchange points
from a battle or at the base,

10:45.519 --> 10:49.190
they become inactive
and cannot gain or lose points.

10:50.066 --> 10:53.527
If an inactive player touches
an opposing team member…

10:53.611 --> 10:55.655
INACTIVE

10:55.738 --> 10:58.074
…the bracelets give them
a tremendous shock.

10:58.574 --> 11:01.243
It could even knock you out,
so be careful.

11:02.328 --> 11:05.831
Once you touch your own base,
you become active again.

11:10.294 --> 11:11.462
Those are the rules.

11:12.171 --> 11:15.007
After you decide how to divide the points,
the game will start.

11:21.472 --> 11:22.306
Wait!

11:26.936 --> 11:27.895
I'm Arisu.

11:30.106 --> 11:31.023
Kyuma.

11:32.817 --> 11:35.486
I want to know something before we begin.

11:38.823 --> 11:40.574
If we clear all the games,

11:43.119 --> 11:44.620
can we return to the real world?

11:48.666 --> 11:51.377
First of all, what is the "real world"?

11:53.462 --> 11:55.673
This "real world" you want to return to…

11:57.216 --> 12:00.636
it seems that you believe
it is the true world.

12:02.555 --> 12:03.722
What do you mean by that?

12:05.683 --> 12:06.767
When you were there,

12:07.268 --> 12:10.020
how many people could you talk to honestly

12:10.563 --> 12:12.815
and deal with truthfully?

12:14.066 --> 12:16.444
Vanity and deception.

12:17.653 --> 12:20.156
Shit like that falls away quickly here.

12:22.324 --> 12:23.742
When faced with death,

12:24.743 --> 12:27.788
that's when you see
the true nature of people.

12:32.918 --> 12:35.588
This world is the real world.

12:36.630 --> 12:38.549
Games are true conversations.

12:40.050 --> 12:45.389
Let's converse with our naked souls
and with all our strength, Arisu!

12:47.183 --> 12:48.934
If you want to know the truth,

12:49.935 --> 12:52.146
then battle me with all your might.

13:04.283 --> 13:05.451
All right.

13:08.454 --> 13:09.580
I'll show you.

13:19.465 --> 13:22.384
You know,
that Kyuma dude seems like a nice guy.

13:23.010 --> 13:24.386
He seemed like a normal person.

13:24.470 --> 13:27.139
How can a buck-naked nutjob be normal?

13:27.681 --> 13:30.142
This is just another fight to the death
like all the others.

13:32.144 --> 13:33.062
Okay.

13:33.604 --> 13:35.439
Let's divide up the points.

13:36.065 --> 13:38.817
How will we divide up the 10,000 points?

13:41.237 --> 13:42.321
How about in five equal parts?

13:42.404 --> 13:45.074
It's way too basic.
We'll never win that way.

13:47.910 --> 13:49.078
Like Kyuma said,

13:49.662 --> 13:50.913
in this game, Osmosis,

13:51.413 --> 13:55.084
the way we divide the points has
a huge impact on who wins.

13:55.876 --> 13:57.336
You got a plan?

14:04.301 --> 14:05.970
DIFFICULTY LEVEL

14:06.053 --> 14:07.930
Game start.

14:40.921 --> 14:41.922
Here's the plan.

14:42.506 --> 14:45.009
The fast runners get
a low number of points

14:45.551 --> 14:47.720
while the slow runners get a lot.

14:49.388 --> 14:53.225
Whoever guards the base gets
the least possible number of points.

14:54.226 --> 14:59.231
We'll split into pairs with one high-point
and one low-point member.

15:00.232 --> 15:02.109
Why did you pair up with me?

15:02.192 --> 15:03.944
I didn't know you liked me so much.

15:04.028 --> 15:06.822
If I have to see you die,
it won't bother me.

15:08.574 --> 15:11.994
The benefit of pairing up is
when you touch an opponent for a battle,

15:12.077 --> 15:14.663
they can only see
your total number of points.

15:14.747 --> 15:18.083
In other words, our opponents won't know
how much each of us has.

15:27.343 --> 15:28.594
NIRAGI: 4,700

15:29.219 --> 15:30.596
USAGI: 300

15:31.764 --> 15:33.641
Combined, we've got 5,000 points.

15:33.724 --> 15:37.895
When splitting 10,000 points among five,
they wouldn't give 5,000 to one person.

15:38.646 --> 15:39.605
Let's fight this guy.

15:40.189 --> 15:41.649
I like that attitude.

15:49.907 --> 15:50.908
I see.

15:57.206 --> 15:59.333
He must not have had much.

16:11.512 --> 16:12.680
Nothing.

16:15.975 --> 16:17.726
No, nothing.

16:24.900 --> 16:27.903
Why the heck
did you pair up Usagi and Niragi?

16:28.612 --> 16:29.571
It's part of the plan.

16:30.656 --> 16:32.116
Did something happen between you?

16:32.616 --> 16:33.659
No. It was nothing.

16:35.119 --> 16:36.036
Arisu.

16:37.746 --> 16:40.165
If it's something
that'll hinder our teamwork,

16:40.249 --> 16:41.750
then shouldn't you talk about it?

16:43.002 --> 16:45.170
That's not it. I did it for a reason.

16:46.380 --> 16:47.631
Fine. Whatever.

16:54.179 --> 16:55.014
That must be it!

17:14.241 --> 17:18.454
KUINA: 300 +2,000
ITEM

17:18.537 --> 17:20.039
KUINA: 2,300

17:21.415 --> 17:22.458
I got 2,000 points!

17:23.375 --> 17:24.209
All right!

17:26.336 --> 17:27.421
Yes!

17:27.504 --> 17:30.591
The Player Team obtained an item.

17:31.383 --> 17:34.386
The Player Team leads by 2,000 points.

17:34.470 --> 17:36.805
- That's 12,000 points!
- We lead by 2,000!

17:40.100 --> 17:41.268
That's a promising start.

17:46.148 --> 17:47.900
Being cautious is boring.

17:48.567 --> 17:49.735
Let's try a battle.

17:52.613 --> 17:53.822
ARISU: 4,600

17:53.906 --> 17:55.824
KUINA: 2,300

18:10.172 --> 18:11.507
Let's stay together.

18:12.007 --> 18:14.718
It's two-on-one,
so there's no need to panic.

18:15.302 --> 18:16.136
Right.

18:19.515 --> 18:23.185
I didn't mean to eavesdrop,
but I couldn't help hearing you.

18:24.394 --> 18:26.271
Did you have a fight
with another team member?

18:33.070 --> 18:33.987
Arisu.

18:35.948 --> 18:37.825
There's a lot of determination
in your eyes.

18:39.409 --> 18:43.664
They tell me you've faced death many times
and are prepared to sacrifice everything.

18:44.623 --> 18:49.628
So it's strange to me
that you'd let something trouble you now.

18:54.591 --> 18:56.510
Our team was originally a band.

18:57.719 --> 19:02.391
Sometimes we'd fight and argue,
but they still stuck with me.

19:02.975 --> 19:06.520
However, there's something
I learned as a leader.

19:07.688 --> 19:10.607
You can't just
randomly lead people around.

19:11.567 --> 19:15.487
You need to listen to their feelings
and wait for them to come around.

19:17.030 --> 19:20.868
When you do that, you'll eventually
come to understand one another.

19:27.166 --> 19:28.000
Okay.

19:29.251 --> 19:30.085
Let's do this.

19:36.842 --> 19:39.386
You could die today, you know?

19:39.928 --> 19:44.016
It's the same for me and my teammates.
Of course, you guys too, Arisu.

19:45.100 --> 19:47.019
So let's not have any regrets.

19:47.519 --> 19:48.729
If we're going to die,

19:49.605 --> 19:51.732
then I want us to fight bravely
before we die.

20:06.121 --> 20:06.997
Arisu…

20:09.625 --> 20:10.626
Kyuma.

20:11.752 --> 20:13.212
Like you said before,

20:14.129 --> 20:18.258
if I want to know the truth,
then I should fight with all my might.

20:19.343 --> 20:20.219
Right.

20:22.429 --> 20:24.431
I want to start
by getting to know you better.

20:25.891 --> 20:27.392
So battle me.

20:33.857 --> 20:34.858
But Arisu…

20:39.196 --> 20:40.489
With pleasure.

20:54.836 --> 20:57.673
ARISU: 4,600 WIN
KYUMA: 2,000 LOSE

20:57.756 --> 20:58.882
Damn!

20:58.966 --> 21:00.259
There has been a change in points

21:00.342 --> 21:01.551
- I lost!
- for both teams.

21:02.135 --> 21:03.053
Two thousand points?

21:03.136 --> 21:04.471
ARISU: 4,600 +500
KYUMA: 2,000 -500

21:04.972 --> 21:07.391
The Player Team leads by 3,000 points.

21:10.894 --> 21:14.273
You mean you divided
your 10,000 points evenly?

21:14.856 --> 21:15.857
That's right.

21:15.941 --> 21:17.693
Each person got 2,000 points.

21:18.485 --> 21:20.320
But this is a deathmatch, right?

21:23.657 --> 21:29.788
To me, my teammates and I are equals
who either live or die together.

21:33.709 --> 21:37.629
Have you come
to know me a little bit better now?

22:11.413 --> 22:12.497
Shit!

22:16.084 --> 22:18.253
Fucking shit! They got me!

22:18.337 --> 22:19.338
Yes!

22:19.421 --> 22:22.341
There has been a change
in points for both teams.

22:24.051 --> 22:27.179
The Player Team leads by 4,000 points.

22:28.597 --> 22:29.681
All right!

22:48.325 --> 22:51.328
There has been a change
in points for both teams.

22:51.411 --> 22:52.412
Yes!

22:52.496 --> 22:54.915
- The Player Team leads by 5,000 points.
- Sorry, man.

22:59.377 --> 23:01.171
You guys are awesome!

23:01.838 --> 23:03.423
It's starting out almost too well.

23:03.507 --> 23:06.426
This guy's a King? What a joke.

23:06.510 --> 23:07.427
High five!

23:07.928 --> 23:09.471
Yes!

23:09.554 --> 23:10.722
I hate to admit it,

23:10.806 --> 23:13.809
but I've almost forgotten
that you're one of the bad guys.

23:30.283 --> 23:31.118
ARISU: INACTIVE

23:33.036 --> 23:34.121
What did you find out?

23:34.621 --> 23:36.832
They split their points evenly.

23:36.915 --> 23:38.125
Evenly?

23:38.208 --> 23:39.960
Two thousand points each.

23:40.460 --> 23:43.380
Let's keep battling them like this
and keep looking for items.

23:45.257 --> 23:47.634
Tatta, I'm counting on you
to protect this.

23:48.135 --> 23:49.052
Sure thing.

24:03.233 --> 24:06.027
They've got a 5,000-point lead on us.

24:06.111 --> 24:07.904
Well, this situation sure sucks.

24:08.572 --> 24:10.907
What are we going to do now, "leader"?

24:12.576 --> 24:14.077
Those guys are pretty damn good.

24:14.578 --> 24:15.787
How can you compliment them?

24:16.329 --> 24:20.041
It's your fault for dividing
the points evenly without any plan at all.

24:20.125 --> 24:21.835
Don't be like that.

24:22.502 --> 24:25.088
There's no majority rule on our team.

24:26.506 --> 24:28.133
Until now,

24:28.216 --> 24:31.761
we've only ever made important decisions
when we all agree what to do.

24:32.554 --> 24:33.722
That's for sure.

24:33.805 --> 24:34.890
Then what will we do?

24:35.724 --> 24:36.725
Come on, Maki!

24:38.018 --> 24:39.394
Why don't you chill out?

24:39.477 --> 24:40.937
And why don't you get serious?

24:43.148 --> 24:45.984
I've got a good idea.

24:46.067 --> 24:47.110
I do too.

24:47.611 --> 24:49.779
It's a freaking crazy idea.

24:51.948 --> 24:54.784
You want to bet we've got the same idea?

24:56.036 --> 24:58.038
Then how about
we say it together on three?

24:58.121 --> 24:59.206
Sure.

25:00.832 --> 25:02.292
- One, two, three!
- One, two, three!

25:06.504 --> 25:09.633
The Player Team obtained an item.

25:11.593 --> 25:14.554
The Player Team leads by 6,000 points.

25:15.680 --> 25:16.848
All right!

25:32.864 --> 25:33.698
Yo.

26:03.228 --> 26:04.771
What did you come here for?

26:04.854 --> 26:06.648
To win, of course.

26:26.001 --> 26:27.627
TATTA: INFINITE

26:30.672 --> 26:31.548
I…

26:32.590 --> 26:35.218
I've got infinite points now.

26:40.682 --> 26:41.683
If I touch you,

26:43.977 --> 26:44.894
you'll die!

26:49.983 --> 26:50.900
That's right.

26:52.027 --> 26:54.195
This is a deathmatch after all.

26:55.280 --> 26:57.282
You choose who dies.

26:58.992 --> 27:02.162
What? That doesn't make any sense!

27:04.164 --> 27:04.998
You'll die!

27:06.791 --> 27:07.751
Stay away!

27:11.004 --> 27:12.005
Stay away!

27:22.140 --> 27:25.518
There has been a change
in points for both teams.

27:30.148 --> 27:33.193
The King of Clubs Team
leads by 4,000 points.

27:33.276 --> 27:34.444
They came from behind.

27:35.987 --> 27:37.364
How did that happen?

27:39.115 --> 27:43.787
In addition, one participant
has less than zero points.

27:53.797 --> 27:54.881
Me, huh?

28:06.309 --> 28:08.144
You guys had better win.

28:09.771 --> 28:11.606
If you waste my death,

28:12.357 --> 28:15.068
I'll beat the shit out of you in heaven.

28:16.277 --> 28:18.905
The game is over for that participant.

28:25.245 --> 28:26.246
Shitara…

28:27.497 --> 28:31.334
I won't ever forget you,
not for a single second.

28:37.215 --> 28:38.216
Later, guys.

29:08.496 --> 29:09.831
Shitara…

29:46.075 --> 29:46.993
Shitara…

30:08.223 --> 30:10.558
By sacrificing one of their teammates,

30:12.143 --> 30:14.646
they now have three members
with over 10,000 points.

30:15.814 --> 30:18.358
You can't even guard the base properly.

30:18.441 --> 30:19.609
Fricking moron.

30:20.193 --> 30:22.403
Losers will always be losers
no matter what.

30:22.487 --> 30:23.822
You useless piece of shit.

30:23.905 --> 30:26.533
Tatta did the best he could
in that situation.

30:26.616 --> 30:27.450
"Did the best he could"?

30:28.034 --> 30:30.578
Anyone else would have tagged Kyuma then!

30:31.120 --> 30:32.914
We underestimated them.

30:33.498 --> 30:37.669
His casual attitude fooled us
and made us forget

30:38.253 --> 30:39.671
that he's a King.

30:39.754 --> 30:42.465
And that this is a deathmatch.

30:44.133 --> 30:47.554
Those guys are more prepared
to sacrifice their lives than we are.

30:48.638 --> 30:50.932
If nothing changes, we'll lose for sure.

30:57.897 --> 30:59.566
We've got just one hour left.

31:02.735 --> 31:05.071
We might still win
if we attack their base.

31:05.154 --> 31:07.490
Impossible, as long as
they defend their base.

31:07.574 --> 31:08.867
Like Niragi says, it's useless.

31:09.367 --> 31:10.743
So what are we supposed to do?

31:11.536 --> 31:15.748
Let's split up,
avoid battles, and get items.

31:16.749 --> 31:18.835
That's the only way for us to survive.

31:19.460 --> 31:20.295
Let's get going.

31:36.185 --> 31:37.186
Not here.

31:44.569 --> 31:48.489
The King of Clubs Team obtained an item.

31:49.866 --> 31:53.202
The King of Clubs team
leads by 4,500 points.

31:53.703 --> 31:55.330
They're not easing up.

32:13.264 --> 32:14.182
Sorry.

32:16.726 --> 32:19.771
There has been a change
in points for both teams.

32:21.689 --> 32:25.360
The King of Clubs Team
leads by 5,500 points.

32:29.656 --> 32:33.076
The King of Clubs Team obtained an item.

32:34.786 --> 32:37.956
The King of Clubs Team
leads by 7,000 points.

32:38.456 --> 32:39.999
We're screwed.

32:50.510 --> 32:51.678
Alone, huh?

32:57.016 --> 32:59.102
Finally, a one-on-one fight.

33:00.603 --> 33:03.856
Sorry, but you won't win
without paying a price.

33:10.363 --> 33:11.948
I'll give you a taste of my fists.

33:13.074 --> 33:16.369
You'll spend the rest of the game
flat on your ass.

33:31.968 --> 33:35.054
KUINA: 3,050
MAKI: 11,500

33:35.138 --> 33:36.139
KUINA: INACTIVE

33:37.724 --> 33:40.977
You should've told me
you knew how to fight.

33:43.271 --> 33:45.815
There has been a change
in points for both teams.

33:45.898 --> 33:47.900
I told them to avoid battles.
What's their problem?

33:47.984 --> 33:50.486
The King of Clubs team leads
by 8,000 points.

34:13.134 --> 34:14.218
Finders keepers.

34:19.640 --> 34:21.601
Yes, 3,000 points!

34:21.684 --> 34:23.686
That's the biggest item.

34:26.481 --> 34:27.440
What's going on?

34:28.149 --> 34:29.400
If you're both here…

34:30.777 --> 34:31.611
You mean

34:32.612 --> 34:34.447
there's nobody at your base?

34:35.031 --> 34:35.865
Yes.

34:36.365 --> 34:37.867
The way you guys are now,

34:37.950 --> 34:41.412
we figured you wouldn't think of
or have the guts to attack our base.

34:43.247 --> 34:44.582
You've got to be kidding…

34:48.878 --> 34:51.130
You said you wanted some answers, right?

34:54.050 --> 34:56.719
Everything about these games
is harsh and ludicrous.

34:57.804 --> 35:00.890
We thought our lives were precious,
but they're snuffed out so easily.

35:01.474 --> 35:04.936
In fact, just now, I lost a close friend.

35:07.522 --> 35:11.275
Shitara was a member of our band.

35:12.318 --> 35:14.695
We lived together in a filthy apartment.

35:16.614 --> 35:18.699
Back then,
we risked our lives to play live.

35:19.700 --> 35:23.955
They were tiny venues,
but they were tons of fun.

35:31.129 --> 35:32.547
When playing these games,

35:34.340 --> 35:37.260
we can see each player's true character.

35:38.761 --> 35:40.304
We're utterly naked.

35:42.265 --> 35:43.558
Just like live shows.

35:46.102 --> 35:47.186
I think…

35:48.855 --> 35:51.858
I wanted to see
the real attitude of people towards life.

35:57.113 --> 35:59.532
Shitara lived admirably until the end.

36:13.296 --> 36:16.048
ARISU: 5,350 LOSE
KYUMA: 13,500 WIN

36:16.132 --> 36:18.050
ARISU: 4,850
KYUMA: 14,000

36:18.134 --> 36:19.051
ARISU: INACTIVE

36:20.469 --> 36:21.470
Arisu.

36:24.807 --> 36:26.225
Don't you dare forget

36:27.810 --> 36:29.729
that this is a deathmatch.

36:31.439 --> 36:32.940
The losers die.

36:36.444 --> 36:38.571
Show me how you want to live life.

36:51.459 --> 36:53.878
Time remaining, 30 minutes.

36:53.961 --> 36:57.840
The King of Clubs Team
leads by 12,000 points.

37:00.676 --> 37:01.510
USAGI: INACTIVE

37:07.934 --> 37:09.352
Only 30 minutes left.

37:09.852 --> 37:11.646
They've got a 12,000-point lead.

37:12.146 --> 37:13.981
It's too soon to give up.

37:14.065 --> 37:15.900
Let's find all the items we can.

37:15.983 --> 37:19.904
There are only 2,500 points in items left.

37:19.987 --> 37:21.405
There must be some other way!

37:22.198 --> 37:24.200
If we don't do anything,
we really will die!

37:24.700 --> 37:26.786
We've still got Tatta with over 10,000.

37:27.453 --> 37:29.956
- We could pair with him and battle.
- The hell I will!

37:31.123 --> 37:33.209
We all know whose fault it is
that this happened.

37:34.043 --> 37:37.129
There isn't any damn job
we can let this loser do.

37:38.798 --> 37:40.883
We're also behind by 12,000 points.

37:41.384 --> 37:45.638
We'll never catch up just by battling
and gaining a measly 500 points each time.

37:49.392 --> 37:50.726
If I were Kyuma…

37:52.478 --> 37:53.396
I'd…

38:00.695 --> 38:04.991
ARISU: INACTIVE

38:05.866 --> 38:07.618
If you want to know the truth,

38:07.702 --> 38:10.371
then battle me with all your might.

38:10.454 --> 38:11.831
When playing these games,

38:13.416 --> 38:16.419
we can see each player's true character.

38:18.129 --> 38:19.922
This is a deathmatch.

38:20.923 --> 38:22.800
Show me how you want to live life.

38:22.883 --> 38:25.386
ARISU: INACTIVE

38:29.098 --> 38:30.850
We'll attack their base.

38:34.687 --> 38:37.982
If two of us can touch their base,
we'll get 20,000 points.

38:38.983 --> 38:40.109
We can win then.

38:40.192 --> 38:41.402
But that's impossible!

38:42.028 --> 38:43.696
I saw it happen myself.

38:44.405 --> 38:47.408
There's no way in hell we could do that!

38:47.491 --> 38:48.868
Then…

38:49.660 --> 38:53.664
let's give the finger to that fear
that's holding us back.

38:54.665 --> 38:56.042
Have you lost your mind?

38:56.834 --> 39:01.339
The difference between us and them
is that we're letting fear hold us back.

39:01.881 --> 39:05.259
So let's tell our fear to fuck off.

39:07.178 --> 39:09.221
That plan's insane.

39:10.723 --> 39:12.641
I can't waste our lives like that.

39:13.392 --> 39:16.896
But if we don't do anything,
we'll all die for sure.

39:17.730 --> 39:19.732
I think it's worth it to risk our lives.

39:21.233 --> 39:22.485
We're a team.

39:23.235 --> 39:24.236
We're teammates.

39:24.987 --> 39:26.822
So I don't want any of us to die.

39:26.906 --> 39:29.575
But I would risk my life

39:30.785 --> 39:32.453
if it would save all of you.

39:34.622 --> 39:36.916
I like your plan. Count me in.

39:41.128 --> 39:43.589
I couldn't give a shit about you people.

39:44.256 --> 39:48.928
But I told my fear to fuck off ages ago.

39:55.226 --> 39:56.227
Me too.

39:58.896 --> 40:01.065
I also want to win this game.

40:04.777 --> 40:06.070
Aw, hell.

40:08.280 --> 40:10.491
I can't let you look like
the only cool one.

40:13.577 --> 40:14.412
I don't think…

40:18.624 --> 40:19.625
Tatta.

40:20.960 --> 40:22.211
You take care of things here.

40:25.464 --> 40:26.382
Okay.

40:40.980 --> 40:44.775
As long as we guard this, we win.

40:53.576 --> 40:54.994
Try and catch me!

40:58.164 --> 41:01.000
Doesn't that chick only have 50 points?

41:02.293 --> 41:04.462
You'll die instantly, you know?

41:08.549 --> 41:10.009
Goken, don't do it!

41:10.092 --> 41:11.844
Don't let her provoke you!

41:13.053 --> 41:15.264
We'll still win.

41:29.653 --> 41:31.614
I haven't been so invigorated in a while!

41:34.825 --> 41:36.577
Time for some fun!

41:52.718 --> 41:53.719
Here's another one.

42:25.668 --> 42:26.502
You guys!

42:27.586 --> 42:31.382
You must be so bored with life
that you're starving for excitement!

42:34.385 --> 42:37.763
You sure do know us well!

42:47.147 --> 42:48.148
KYUMA: INFINITE

42:48.232 --> 42:49.483
MAKI: INFINITE

42:50.067 --> 42:51.318
UTA: INFINITE

42:52.278 --> 42:53.696
You guys will die!

44:08.687 --> 44:09.813
Here I come!

44:11.357 --> 44:12.316
Okay.

45:08.664 --> 45:10.082
ARISU: INACTIVE

45:13.919 --> 45:15.087
You're inactive?

45:29.476 --> 45:32.688
The Player Team has gained points.

45:34.773 --> 45:35.649
Yes!

45:35.732 --> 45:36.567
Just 10,000 more!

45:37.151 --> 45:37.985
NIRAGI: INACTIVE

45:38.068 --> 45:39.278
Niragi!

45:45.284 --> 45:46.326
Kuina!

45:47.786 --> 45:48.996
Go!

46:00.716 --> 46:03.802
There has been a change
in points for both teams.

46:05.846 --> 46:09.183
The King of Clubs Team
leads by 3,000 points.

46:20.277 --> 46:22.988
Congrats on getting 10,000 points!

46:24.364 --> 46:25.824
You're really something, Arisu.

46:25.908 --> 46:27.534
That was a good plan.

46:28.410 --> 46:29.953
But it's over for you guys.

46:31.163 --> 46:35.334
Even if you find the last item,
you won't have enough.

46:38.462 --> 46:41.048
You won't ever get that chance again.

46:41.632 --> 46:44.384
Until time runs out,
we'll stay by this base

46:45.928 --> 46:47.179
and never do battle.

46:47.679 --> 46:50.057
Time remaining, 20 minutes.

46:50.849 --> 46:54.520
The King of Clubs Team
leads by 3,000 points.

47:14.248 --> 47:15.249
I'm sorry.

47:17.668 --> 47:18.919
It's all my fault.

47:22.714 --> 47:23.757
No, it's not.

47:25.342 --> 47:27.219
We all did our very best.

47:29.513 --> 47:31.348
My idea wasn't good enough.

47:32.516 --> 47:33.433
I'm sorry.

47:36.353 --> 47:37.646
Everyone takes the blame, huh?

47:42.067 --> 47:44.820
It's your fucking fault we'll all die!

47:56.915 --> 47:58.375
I'll look for the item.

47:59.418 --> 48:00.752
It's too late now.

48:01.795 --> 48:03.547
Maybe this is just to please myself,

48:05.757 --> 48:06.675
but…

48:10.554 --> 48:11.722
I want to do everything I can

48:13.390 --> 48:14.891
to the very end.

48:26.528 --> 48:27.738
She sure is tough.

48:30.157 --> 48:31.575
I could never do that.

49:07.611 --> 49:10.197
All that crap about cooperating
was such bullshit.

49:14.034 --> 49:15.911
Fucking self-righteous bastards.

49:18.580 --> 49:19.498
Fuck it all!

49:31.093 --> 49:32.678
I was such a fool.

49:44.272 --> 49:48.193
I don't have much time anyway.

50:41.496 --> 50:42.664
There must be…

50:43.165 --> 50:44.666
There must be a way.

50:59.806 --> 51:00.849
I found it!

51:11.902 --> 51:14.988
The Player Team obtained an item.

51:17.532 --> 51:20.452
The King of Clubs Team
leads by 500 points.

51:22.120 --> 51:23.830
Usagi got the item.

51:26.792 --> 51:28.126
Only 500 more points.

51:29.252 --> 51:30.295
I've got to do something.

51:31.171 --> 51:32.380
I've got to do something!

51:35.884 --> 51:37.677
I'll go to Kyuma's base.

51:37.761 --> 51:38.595
Why?

51:39.095 --> 51:42.098
We just need 500 points.
Some kind of miracle could happen!

51:43.099 --> 51:44.142
That's ridiculous.

51:44.226 --> 51:47.562
If I'm going to die anyway,
I want to do everything I can before I do!

51:48.438 --> 51:49.481
Arisu…

51:54.027 --> 51:57.280
Come to think of it, I never did tell you.

52:00.534 --> 52:01.576
Tatta…

52:03.286 --> 52:07.541
You've always been so optimistic.
You've really cheered me up.

52:12.420 --> 52:13.463
Thank you.

52:26.893 --> 52:29.145
Time remaining, ten minutes.

52:29.229 --> 52:32.315
The King of Clubs Team
leads by 500 points.

52:32.399 --> 52:33.316
We can still win.

52:42.367 --> 52:43.201
Niragi?

52:54.462 --> 52:56.047
Pretty pitiful, huh?

52:57.215 --> 52:58.800
I found the item!

52:58.884 --> 53:00.218
We just need 500 more points!

53:00.302 --> 53:01.511
Don't be stupid.

53:02.762 --> 53:04.264
I'm not giving up.

53:11.021 --> 53:12.439
We're going to die.

53:13.481 --> 53:15.150
Both you and I are going to die.

53:17.652 --> 53:19.571
I've got no hope left.

53:25.493 --> 53:27.078
You people…

53:27.704 --> 53:30.832
you've always got
a righteous look on your faces.

53:35.754 --> 53:37.505
Do I really disgust you that much?

53:38.548 --> 53:39.424
Do I?

53:41.259 --> 53:43.762
Everyone looks at me that way.

53:53.188 --> 53:56.942
I don't know if everyone hated me
because I was twisted,

53:58.526 --> 54:02.530
or if I became twisted
because everyone hated me.

54:06.159 --> 54:07.702
Remember what Kyuma said?

54:09.955 --> 54:12.874
We can see a person's true character
in the face of death.

54:15.752 --> 54:16.836
I finally understand

54:17.629 --> 54:18.880
after facing death.

54:20.715 --> 54:23.468
I'm not like you people
who take the blame for others.

54:25.261 --> 54:28.181
I'm not the kind of person
who clings to hopes and dreams.

54:30.642 --> 54:31.726
I'm scum.

54:56.584 --> 54:59.421
I can finally pick up where we left off.

55:01.297 --> 55:02.882
Let's have a good fuck

55:02.966 --> 55:05.969
and face the end of our lives
with a smile on our faces!

55:15.020 --> 55:16.104
Usagi!

55:20.150 --> 55:21.067
Arisu!

55:22.068 --> 55:23.069
Shut up!

55:37.500 --> 55:39.586
Time remaining, nine minutes.

55:40.128 --> 55:43.173
The King of Clubs Team
leads by 500 points.

58:53.279 --> 58:58.284
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
